.TH GLEAN 1 "2026-07-05" "glean 0.7.0-proto" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
glean \- turn command output into data
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glean run
[\fB--\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIargs...\fR]
.br
.I command
|
.B glean
[\fB--silent\fR] [\fB--min-confidence\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB--sync\fR]
.br
.B glean
\fIsubcommand\fR [\fIargs...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B glean
captures a command's output, auto-detects its format (via a library of 200+
extract strategies), and presents it as a tidy, one-row-per-record dataset in a
git-backed store. Every capture is a commit; every dataset row carries a
globally-unique index so it can be traced back to its source.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B run [--] \fIcommand\fR [args...]
Execute a command, capture its combined output as a commit, auto-detect the
format, and file it into a typed dataset.
.TP
.I command
| \fBglean\fR [\fB--silent\fR] [\fB--min-confidence\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB--sync\fR]
Inject piped/stdin (or a FILE argument) the same way as
.BR run .
By default the capture runs in a detached background process and the prompt
returns at once; results appear in
.B glean log
shortly after. \fB--sync\fR/\fB--wait\fR (or \fBGLEAN_ASYNC=0\fR) forces the
foreground path, which prints the resulting dataset and \fI#N\fR range.
.TP
.B source \fI#N\fR
Show the original captured input behind dataset row \fI#N\fR.
.TP
.B control \fR[\fIdir\fR]
Make \fIdir\fR (default: cwd) its own capture instance; captures run inside it
route there, and each commit snapshots the directory's contents as context.
.TP
.B uncontrol \fR[\fIdir\fR]
Release a controlled directory (its data is kept).
.TP
.B instances
List controlled directories.
.TP
.B export \fR[\fIfile\fR]
Bundle the whole store (datasets + capture commits) into a portable file.
.TP
.B import \fIfile\fR \fR[\fIdest\fR]
Reconstitute a bundle elsewhere to browse.
.TP
.B log
List captures (the git history).
.TP
.B restore \fI#id\fR|latest
Bring a capture's commit back up; \fBlatest\fR returns to the tip.
.TP
.B ls
List datasets.
.TP
.B show \fINAME\fR
Present a dataset as a tidy table (leading \fB#N\fR is the row index).
For the \fBunsorted\fR bucket the base64 \fBraw\fR column is decoded to text.
.TP
.B rm [\fB-f\fR|\fB--yes\fR] [\fB--no-purge\fR] \fINAME\fR...
Delete one or more datasets. Removes each named dataset file, prunes its rows
from the provenance map, and commits the deletion (the git history and
\fBrestore\fR still reach the pre-deletion state). By default it also purges the
captures that fed the removed dataset(s); \fB--no-purge\fR/\fB--keep-captures\fR
keeps them. Prompts unless \fB-f\fR/\fB--yes\fR. Aliases: \fBdelete\fR, \fBdrop\fR.
.TP
.B stats \fINAME\fR [analyze-args]
Statistics on a dataset (\fB--all\fR for every analysis).
.TP
.B triage
Show the low-confidence / unmatched bucket, raw input decoded to text
(\fBglean source #N\fR for the exact original bytes).
.TP
.B doctor
Check the extract/analyze engines and the store.
.SH STORE
By default captures go to a global git store at
.BR $GLEAN_HOME ", or " ~/.glean
if unset, so you can capture from any directory. Point
.B GLEAN_HOME
at a shared, group-writable directory to collaborate; a lock serialises
concurrent writers. A controlled directory (see
.BR control )
overrides the global store while you are inside it.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GLEAN_HOME
Global store directory (default: ~/.glean).
.TP
.B GLEAN_WORKSPACE
Explicit store override (wins over GLEAN_HOME).
.TP
.B GLEAN_MIN_CONFIDENCE
Commit threshold 0\-100 (default: 50).
.TP
.B GLEAN_ASYNC
Background capture (default 1). Set 0 (or pass \fB--sync\fR/\fB--wait\fR) for the
foreground path.
.TP
.B GLEAN_MAX_INPUT
Maximum input bytes (default: 10485760).
.TP
.B GLEAN_LOCK_TIMEOUT
Seconds to wait for the store lock (default: 30).
.TP
.B GLEAN_RECONCILE_OVERLAP
Percent column overlap to union (vs split a variant) on schema drift (default: 60).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
free -m | glean                 # capture + auto-detect + file
glean run df -h                 # capture a command as a commit
glean ls                        # list datasets
glean show df                   # present as a tidy table
glean source 5                  # original input behind row #5
glean stats df                  # statistics on the dataset
glean export ~/store.bundle     # portable export
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
The glean prototype is documented in
.IR docs/proposals/0001-glean-rename-and-simplification.md .
